      "content": "that makes sense. i think we also need to address the more extreme side of things. sometimes, patients in the ED can get these strange, frenetic energies—they might even start acting almost... creature-like or primitive in their outbursts, just wildly erratic and hard to contain. how should staff maintain professional boundaries when a patient's behavior feels that unhinged and almost non-human?",
